# Team Workflow (ai-avengers, 3 members)

## Default model: solo-driver + squad
- Lead Developer: primary Cursor driver
- Data & Content QA: dataset, speakers, venues, a11y review
- Ship & Story: deploy, README, augmentation log, video, demo backup

## Branching
- Short-lived branches; Ship owner merges to default after Tier 2 pass
- One logical slice per commit message
- Tag `demo-submission` on final submission commit

## Augmentation log (one entry per completed run)
Log **once** when a full plan execution finishes, all agents are idle, and WSL validation is done — not per phase or per turn. See `ai-augmentation.mdc`. A plan run is **not complete** until the entry exists.

## Entry owner
Lead Developer (or whoever ran the Cursor prompt) owns the entry; Ship & Story reviews completeness before MR. **MR / ship-branch gate:** do not open an MR for a plan branch until the augmentation-log entry exists.

## Prompt hygiene
- Reference relevant .mdc rules in every build prompt
- Include "do not break docker/CI" when touching pubspec or docker files
- Include "web-only" when adding packages

## Review hygiene
- Verify every cited file path exists (`Read`/`Grep`) before applying a diff
- Verify package/SDK versions cited match `pubspec.lock`
- Verify referenced route paths appear in `lib/routing/app_router.dart`
- Verify dataset field names appear in `assets/data/schema/*.json`
- Verify test counts claimed match `flutter test` output
- If a suggestion touches a file listed in `parallel-agents.mdc` forbidden shared surface, treat as a serial-merge patch note
- When `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` files are touched, verify catalog parity per `cursor-rules-catalog.mdc` (mdc count = slug.md count) before MR
- Log every hallucination found during review in `augmentation-log.md` `Hallucinations` field, even when the overall `Outcome` is `accepted`
